title: Counting
mode: vhdl
chapter: Memory
check: behaves
cycles: 200
random: rst=0.03
---- intro
A **counter** is a register that adds 1 to itself on every clock edge: 0, 1, 2 ... 15, and then round to 0. It is how a circuit measures time, or steps through the instructions of a program.

An output cannot be read inside the architecture, so the count is kept in a **signal**, `count` (an `unsigned` number, declared for you), and connected to `q`:

```
process (clk)
begin
    if rising_edge(clk) then
        count <= count + 1;
    end if;
end process;
q <= std_logic_vector(count);
```

This one also has a reset: when `rst` is 1 at a clock edge, the count goes back to 0.
---- task
Count up by one on every clock edge, back to 0 when `rst` is 1; `q` is the count.
---- start
library ieee;
use ieee.std_logic_1164.all;
use ieee.numeric_std.all;

entity counter is
  port(
    clk : in  std_logic;
    rst : in  std_logic;
    q   : out std_logic_vector(3 downto 0)
  );
end counter;

architecture rtl of counter is
    signal count : unsigned(3 downto 0) := (others => '0');
begin
    -- write it here
end rtl;
---- answer
library ieee;
use ieee.std_logic_1164.all;
use ieee.numeric_std.all;

entity counter is
  port(
    clk : in  std_logic;
    rst : in  std_logic;
    q   : out std_logic_vector(3 downto 0)
  );
end counter;

architecture rtl of counter is
    signal count : unsigned(3 downto 0) := (others => '0');
begin
    process (clk)
    begin
        if rising_edge(clk) then
            if rst = '1' then
                count <= (others => '0');
            else
                count <= count + 1;
            end if;
        end if;
    end process;
    q <= std_logic_vector(count);
end rtl;
---- hint1
Start from the process in the text, and add the reset with `if rst = '1' then ... else ... end if;` inside it.
---- hint2
`(others => '0')` is "all bits 0". Inside the clock edge: `if rst = '1' then count <= (others => '0'); else count <= count + 1; end if;`
---- solution
```
process (clk)
begin
    if rising_edge(clk) then
        if rst = '1' then
            count <= (others => '0');
        else
            count <= count + 1;
        end if;
    end if;
end process;
q <= std_logic_vector(count);
```
---- done
Your circuit counts: flip-flops remembering the count and an adder adding 1, all from one `+`. From a switch and a light to here: these are the parts every processor is made of.
